Technically this attaches the {po'o} to {.ebu} which is undesirable.
Moreover there is a semantic problem with binding an existential variable
to a constant variable. (It isn't so bad when there is only one layer of
quantification but it is catastrophic otherwise.) But there's a simpler
approach:

{.i ky linji .abu ce .ebu}

or if you want a variable:

{.i ky linji ko'a goi .abu ce .ebu}

or if you want the referents first:

{.i ky linji .abu ce .ebu vu'o goi ko'a}

Using {cmima} precisely winds up being awkward because you have to do
something like:

{.i ca'e ro da zo'u da cmima ko'a .i jo da cmima .abu ce .ebu}

mi'e la latro'a mu'o

